{"model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are a Python coding agent. Work in the current directory.\n\n# Task\n\nYou are given positive integers n and target.\nAn array nums is beautiful if it meets the following conditions:\n\nnums.length == n.\nnums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers.\nThere doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, in the range [0, n - 1], such that nums[i] + nums[j] == target.\n\nReturn the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: n = 2, target = 3\nOutput: 4\nExplanation: We can see that nums = [1,3] is beautiful.\n- The array nums has length n = 2.\n- The array nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers.\n- There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, with nums[i] + nums[j] == 3.\nIt can be proven that 4 is the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: n = 3, target = 3\nOutput: 8\nExplanation: We can see that nums = [1,3,4] is beautiful.\n- The array nums has length n = 3.\n- The array nums consists of pairwise distinct positive integers.\n- There doesn't exist two distinct indices, i and j, with nums[i] + nums[j] == 3.\nIt can be proven that 8 is the minimum possible sum that a beautiful array could have.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: n = 1, target = 1\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: We can see, that nums = [1] is beautiful.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= n <= 10^9\n1 <= target <= 10^9\n\n\u8acb\u5beb\u4e00\u500b\u9802\u5c64 Python \u51fd\u5f0f\uff08\u4e0d\u8981\u7528 class\uff09\uff1a\ndef minimumPossibleSum(n: int, target: int):\n\u53ea\u80fd\u7528\u6a19\u6e96\u51fd\u5f0f\u5eab\u3002\u51fd\u5f0f\u5fc5\u9808\u56de\u50b3\u7b54\u6848\uff0c\u4e0d\u8981\u5370\u51fa\u3002\n\n## Entry point\n\nDefine a function named `minimumPossibleSum` in a file called `solution.py` in the\ncurrent directory. It must handle the argument types shown in the checks\nbelow.\n\n## Visible acceptance checks\n\nThe following checks are run against `solution.py` when this process exits:\n\n```\n- `minimumPossibleSum(2, 3) == 4`\n- `minimumPossibleSum(3, 3) == 8`\n- `minimumPossibleSum(1, 1) == 1`\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Write the complete `solution.py` in the current directory.\n- If a file named `VACANT_FEEDBACK.md` exists in the current directory,\n  read it first: it is acceptance feedback from a previous attempt.\n- Do not write any other files.\n\n\nWrite the complete file solution.py in the current directory, defining the required entry-point function.\nReply with the full content of solution.py inside exactly one ```python code block. No prose outside the code block."}], "max_tokens": 8192, "temperature": 0}